 ## Overview
-This method compresses trained 3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS) models by quantizing un-activated parameters and applying image codecs to the resulting grids. It solves the problem of large storage sizes in 3DGS by reducing precision and exploiting spatial redundancy in SH coefficients. It differs from sibling methods like [LightGaussian / CompGS / RDOGS](13540-lightgaussian-compgs-rdogs.md) by using fixed linear quantization ranges derived from dataset percentiles and JPEG XL for storage, rather than learned vector quantization or entropy coding of indices.
